ard \"strongly opposes\" HB 1608. The resolution's own description of that bill is that it would \"require notification to, and approval from, parents\" for name and pronoun changes. So the resolution puts her against rungs 4 and 5. But opposing a state bill neither forbids notification rules (rung 2) nor requires keeping the change from parents (rung 1). It also doesn't separate those rungs from rung 3 (tell parents when they ask). That makes it `direction-only`, so `rests_on` is empty.\n- **No vote tally:** the page shows only the seven signatures, with no roll call. The record is coded as a signed act, not a vote, and I could not check it against the near-unanimous rule.\n- **`needs_source`:**\n  - the board's minutes and roll call for the 28 March 2023 meeting;\n  - any MCCSC board policy vote on telling parents about name or pronoun changes.\n- **Quotes:** none. The resolution speaks in the board's voice, not in her own words.\n\nSome connectors could not be used this session, though the task needed none of them:\n- **Not authorised:** Benevity, Candid, Canva, Figma, Givebutter, Harvey and WorkOS need authorising in the claude.ai connector settings.\n- **Failed to connect:** the GitHub plugin (it returned a bad-authorization error).","ttft_ms":13725,"type":"result","duration_ms":29905,"uuid":"03550dd3-1725-494f-bf9c-3ce02213924e","ttft_stream_ms":1410,"time_to_request_ms":74,"first_content_frame_ms":1410,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
